Package: com.andi.nodejs
Name: Node.js
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Maintainer: andi <tafilajandi@gmail.com>
Author: OpenJS Foundation (upstream) / iOS port by andi
Section: Development
Priority: optional
Depends: zsh, bash, python3, ldid, curl, tar, gzip, coreutils, firmware (>= 15.0)
Conflicts: io.github.imcynic.nodejs
Replaces: io.github.imcynic.nodejs
Icon: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/@REPO@/main/assets/icon.png
Native-Depiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
SileoDepiction: https://@PAGES@/depiction.json
Tag: role::developer
Description: Node.js @NODE_VERSION@ with npm and working nvm, patched for iOS
 A current Node.js on a jailbroken iPhone, with npm, npx and nvm.
 .
 Node is not cross-compiled here. The official darwin-arm64 build from
 nodejs.org imports 725 symbols and iOS is missing exactly three of them, so
 this package downloads Apple's own build, rewrites its Mach-O to claim
 platform iOS, points the two framework load paths at the flat iOS layout, and
 links in a small shim for what is left. The binary is verified against the
 SHA-256 this package was built against before anything is patched.
 .
 The shim is what makes V8 run. iOS rejects MAP_JIT and kills a process that
 executes a writable page, and pthread_jit_write_protect_np -- the call V8's
 arm64 Darwin build uses to flip its code pages -- does not exist on iOS at
 all. The shim strips MAP_JIT, remembers the region, and implements the flip
 with mprotect. That flip is process-wide where the real API is per-thread, so
 the shim also forces V8 --single-threaded, which is the one setting that
 survives a `#!/usr/bin/env node` shebang and anything npm spawns.
 .
 It also remaps /bin/sh and friends into the bootstrap prefix, because a
 rootless jailbreak has no /bin/sh and Node hard-codes it for `shell: true` --
 without which execSync and every npm lifecycle script fail with ENOENT.
 .
 nvm works too. Source nodeios.sh from your shell profile: it corrects nvm's
 architecture detection, which otherwise reads the device model out of
 `uname -m` and asks nodejs.org for a darwin-iPhone16,1 build, and it patches
 each version nvm installs. Node 24 and newer only; 23 and earlier use a Mach-O
 bind format this port cannot rewrite.
 .
 Known limit: worker_threads is reliable up to two workers. Beyond that the
 process-wide W^X flip races and the process takes SIGBUS. Run with
 NODEIOS_V8_FLAGS=--jitless for worker-heavy work, which is slower but safe.
